      "updated": 1766910820156,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Alright so now let's understand  the core of spring security and how we can \nuse it ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Alright so now let's understand  the core of spring security and how we can \nuse it ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "cl8Zt2lJRfUry-31rn4l8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 489.68631349370503,
      "y": 7881.501427488098,
      "width": 712.799560546875,
      "height": 45,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bfB",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1487446369,
      "version": 59,
      "versionNonce": 742246511,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1766910868814,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Internal Working of Spring Security ",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Internal Working of Spring Security ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "vzmV05-dfcwcwOP7lu3Aw",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 494.2197395707665,
      "y": 7939.543164061464,
      "width": 1002.9737481755081,
      "height": 850,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bfD",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 483320033,
      "version": 165,
      "versionNonce": 2014699727,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1766910987717,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1.Authentication\n\nAuthentication is the process of verifying who you are. In a Spring Boot application, this\ninvolves checking your credentials (like a username and password) against the stored data,\nand if they match, you're granted access to the system, much like being allowed into a mall\nafter showing a valid ID.\n\nImagine :\n\nYou're logging into any of your social media apps. Here's how the authentication process\nworks:\n\ni.You open the app and enter your username and password.\n\nii.This is like providing your credentials to the application, which the system will use to\nverify your identity.\n\niii.After entering your credentials, you click the \"Login\" button.\n\niv.The app sends your username and password to the server for verification.\n\nv.The server checks if the provided credentials match the stored records.\n\nvi.If the credentials are correct, the server confirms your identity.\n\nvii.Once verified, you gain access to your account and can start using the app.\n\nviii.The server grants access, allowing you to interact with different features like\nviewing your profile or messaging friends.\n\nix.If the credentials are incorrect, the server denies access and might show an error\nmessage like \"Invalid username or password.”\n\nx.You remain unauthenticated and are not allowed to proceed into the app.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1.Authentication\n\nAuthentication is the process of verifying who you are. In a Spring Boot application, this involves checking your credentials (like a username and password) against the stored data, and if they match, you're granted access to the system, much like being allowed into a mall after showing a valid ID.\n\nImagine :\n\nYou're logging into any of your social media apps. Here's how the authentication process works:\n\ni.You open the app and enter your username and password.\n\nii.This is like providing your credentials to the application, which the system will use to verify your identity.\n\niii.After entering your credentials, you click the \"Login\" button.\n\niv.The app sends your username and password to the server for verification.\n\nv.The server checks if the provided credentials match the stored records.\n\nvi.If the credentials are correct, the server confirms your identity.\n\nvii.Once verified, you gain access to your account and can start using the app.\n\nviii.The server grants access, allowing you to interact with different features like viewing your profile or messaging friends.\n\nix.If the credentials are incorrect, the server denies access and might show an error message like \"Invalid username or password.”\n\nx.You remain unauthenticated and are not allowed to proceed into the app.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "V9CCHQw-wvO0AptZA08LE",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 479.77824384228114,
      "y": 7939.2325389683065,
      "width": 1140.3013822282653,
      "height": 878.2187432691662,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
