    {
      "id": "uRpAKIRuqmJH15ExNTnpT",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -408.47563809769144,
      "y": 99910.56487625708,
      "width": 1076.5664420570404,
      "height": 735,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "blO",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2128135087,
      "version": 96,
      "versionNonce": 310734831,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1767018366903,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🔑 The 3 things that matter (ONLY these)\n\nSpring Security looks at:\n\n1️⃣ The Authentication object class\n2️⃣ The providers registered\n3️⃣ supports(authentication.getClass())\n\n1️⃣ What Authentication object are YOU creating?\n\nIn your login API:\n\nAuthentication auth =\n    new UsernamePasswordAuthenticationToken(username, password);\n\n\nThis is CRITICAL.\n\nYou are literally telling Spring:\n\n\"This is a UsernamePasswordAuthenticationToken\"",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🔑 The 3 things that matter (ONLY these)\n\nSpring Security looks at:\n\n1️⃣ The Authentication object class\n2️⃣ The providers registered\n3️⃣ supports(authentication.getClass())\n\n1️⃣ What Authentication object are YOU creating?\n\nIn your login API:\n\nAuthentication auth =\n    new UsernamePasswordAuthenticationToken(username, password);\n\n\nThis is CRITICAL.\n\nYou are literally telling Spring:\n\n\"This is a UsernamePasswordAuthenticationToken\"",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
