    {
      "id": "JWa-LdkbRNe0mxv3atPsQ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -850.6070333275396,
      "y": 114959.00284226701,
      "width": 769.999755859375,
      "height": 840,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bmR",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1396768289,
      "version": 97,
      "versionNonce": 2059491681,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "CArcbK8PmJXytKAVWczga",
          "type": "arrow"
        },
        {
          "id": "2T5R4h_XpLaqUOPjofa6D",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1767020853588,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Your code (anchor)\n\n@PostMapping(\"/login\")\npublic String login(@RequestBody LoginRequest req)\n{\n\n    Authentication auth =\n        authenticationManager.authenticate(\n            new\nUsernamePasswordAuthenticationToken(\n                req.getUsername(),\n                req.getPassword()\n            )\n        );\n\n    return jwtUtil.generateToken(auth.getName());\n}\n\n\nYou’re asking:\n\n“I’m clearly creating\nUsernamePasswordAuthenticationToken myself — so\nwhere is Spring creating it internally?”",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Your code (anchor)\n\n@PostMapping(\"/login\")\npublic String login(@RequestBody LoginRequest req) {\n\n    Authentication auth =\n        authenticationManager.authenticate(\n            new UsernamePasswordAuthenticationToken(\n                req.getUsername(),\n                req.getPassword()\n            )\n        );\n\n    return jwtUtil.generateToken(auth.getName());\n}\n\n\nYou’re asking:\n\n“I’m clearly creating UsernamePasswordAuthenticationToken myself — so where is Spring creating it internally?”",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
