      "seed": 297563215,
      "version": 40,
      "versionNonce": 561043265,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1767022865168,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "4️⃣ How Spring Auto-Picks Your Provider 🔥\n\nInternally, Spring does:\n\nfor (AuthenticationProvider provider : providers) {\n    if (provider.supports(authentication.getClass())) {\n        return provider.authenticate(authentication);\n    }\n}\n\n\nSo when you pass:\n\nnew MyAuthToken(...)\n\n\nSpring asks:\n\n“Which provider supports this token?”\n\n✔ MyAuthProvider.supports(MyAuthToken.class) → TRUE\n❌ All others → FALSE\n\n➡️ Your provider is selected",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "4️⃣ How Spring Auto-Picks Your Provider 🔥\n\nInternally, Spring does:\n\nfor (AuthenticationProvider provider : providers) {\n    if (provider.supports(authentication.getClass())) {\n        return provider.authenticate(authentication);\n    }\n}\n\n\nSo when you pass:\n\nnew MyAuthToken(...)\n\n\nSpring asks:\n\n“Which provider supports this token?”\n\n✔ MyAuthProvider.supports(MyAuthToken.class) → TRUE\n❌ All others → FALSE\n\n➡️ Your provider is selected",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
